        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "refactor(config): split help quality fixtures",
        "body": "Related: #110218, #110238\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe grandfathered max-lines suppression on the config-help quality test leaves more than 1,100 lines of assertion logic and static target data in one frequently edited file.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis maintainer-requested follow-up moves the unchanged target sets into a colocated test-fixtures module. The assertion body and every target declaration remain byte-identical, while the obsolete suppression and ratchet baseline entry are removed.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo user-visible behavior changes. Maintainers get a smaller assertion module, a cohesive fixture-data boundary, and one fewer grandfathered max-lines exception.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Declaration/body identity probe: all six extracted declarations and the complete assertion body are byte-identical to `origin/main`.\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/config/schema.help.quality.test.ts test/scripts/check-max-lines-ratchet.test.ts` — 2 files, 35 tests passed after rebase.\n- `./node_modules/.bin/oxfmt --check ...`, targeted `node scripts/run-oxlint.mjs ...`, `node scripts/check-max-lines-ratchet.mjs`, and `git diff origin/main...HEAD --check` — passed.\n- `node scripts/check-changed.mjs -- config/max-lines-baseline.txt src/config/schema.help.quality.test.ts src/config/schema.help.quality.test-fixtures.ts` — passed on Blacksmith Testbox: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29622700436\n- `.agents/skills/autoreview/scripts/autoreview --mode branch --base origin/main` — clean; no accepted/actionable findings.\n\nAI-assisted; maintainer reviewed the complete test, fixture data, max-lines ratchet, and surrounding config-help consumers.\n",
